---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import LineIcon from "../components/LineIcon.astro";

const jsonLd = [
  {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
    "itemListElement": [
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 1,
        "name": "Home",
        "item": "https://www.alluviumbi.com/"
      },
      {
        "@type": "ListItem",
        "position": 2,
        "name": "Services",
        "item": "https://www.alluviumbi.com/services"
      }
    ]
  }
];
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Power BI services | Alluvium"
  description="Power BI services for mid-sized companies that already have Power BI or Excel and still cannot get one number the meeting will stand behind."
  canonicalPath="/services"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="service-fold service-hub">
<header class="hero"><div class="wrap">
<nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><span aria-hidden="true"> / </span><span>Services</span></nav>
<p class="kicker">Offerings</p>
<h1>Power BI services</h1>
<p class="lede">This is for mid-sized companies that already have Power BI or Excel, and that still cannot get one number the meeting will stand behind.</p>
</div></header>
<section class="band band-alt"><div class="wrap">
<article class="card-feature card-quickstart">
<svg class="icon-line" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.85" stroke-linecap="round"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="8"/><path d="M12 7.5v4.7l3.2 2"/></svg>
<h2>Power BI Quickstart</h2>
<p>One report that someone rebuilds by hand is replaced in two weeks, with training and one week of support.</p>
<p class="see"><a class="btn" href="/power-bi-quickstart">See Power BI Quickstart</a></p>
</article>
<div class="cards-2">
<article class="card"><svg class="icon-line" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.85" stroke-linecap="round"><circle cx="5" cy="17" r="1.7"/><path d="M6.5 16.1 10.2 10.5"/><circle cx="11.2" cy="9.4" r="1.7"/><path d="M12.7 8.6 16.2 5.8"/><circle cx="18" cy="5.2" r="1.8"/><path d="M4.5 20.5h15"/></svg>
<h2>Analytics strategy roadmap</h2>
<p>You already own the tools, and every team still asks for its own report. We write the order of work so your team knows what to do first and what can wait.</p>
<p class="see"><a href="/analytics-ai-strategy-roadmap">See the analytics strategy roadmap</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><svg class="icon-line" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.85" stroke-linecap="round"><rect x="4.5" y="3.75" width="15" height="16.5" rx="1"/><path d="M8 9.2 9.3 10.5 12.1 7.7"/><path d="M13.2 9.2h3.8M8 13h8M8 16.4h6.4"/></svg>
<h2>Data project management</h2>
<p>The dashboard project stalls because nobody owns the decisions. You get a named owner, a scope that stays put, and a report the business actually opens.</p>
<p class="see"><a href="/data-project-management-change-leadership">See data project management</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><svg class="icon-line" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.85"><rect x="3.8" y="3.8" width="7.2" height="7.2"/><rect x="13" y="3.8" width="7.2" height="7.2"/><rect x="3.8" y="13" width="7.2" height="7.2"/><rect x="13" y="13" width="7.2" height="7.2"/></svg>
<h2>Dashboard optimization</h2>
<p>You paid for a report, and the meeting still goes back to Excel. We revise that report so people can find the number and trust it.</p>
<p class="see"><a href="/power-bi-dashboard-optimization-ai-insights">See dashboard optimization</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><svg class="icon-line" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.85" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M7 6.4A7 7 0 1 0 18.2 12"/><path d="M18.2 12 20.4 8.8M18.2 12l-3.4-.4"/></svg>
<h2>Managed advisory retainer</h2>
<p>After the project ends, the report goes stale or splits into copies. We keep one current version, without hiring a large team to watch it.</p>
<p class="see"><a href="/managed-advisory-retainer">See the managed advisory retainer</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><svg class="icon-line" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.85" stroke-linecap="round"><circle cx="8.6" cy="8" r="2.4"/><path d="M4.2 18.7c.5-3.1 2.2-4.6 4.4-4.6s3.9 1.5 4.4 4.6"/><circle cx="16.2" cy="8.8" r="2"/><path d="M14 18.7c.3-2.2 1.6-3.4 3.1-3.4 1.6 0 2.8 1.2 3.1 3.4"/></svg>
<h2>Power BI Training</h2>
<p>A generic class does not prepare people for the report they open on Monday. We train on that report, so the team can use it and change it when the question changes.</p>
<p class="see"><a href="/power-bi-training">See Power BI training</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><svg class="icon-line" viewBox="0 0 24 24" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.85" stroke-linecap="round"><path d="M5 16.2h14M7 18.4h10M9 20.6h6"/><path d="M5.2 4.2h9.6v6.2L11.6 8.4H5.2z"/></svg>
<h2>Conversational analytics</h2>
<p>People want to ask a plain question and get the number the report already shows. The question goes to the reports you trust, and the answer matches the meeting.</p>
<p class="see"><a href="/conversational-analytics">See conversational analytics</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><LineIcon name="connect" />
<h2>Power BI Migration</h2>
<p>The stack you are leaving gets rebuilt on Power BI, with measures, grain, and an owner. It is not a converter that copies the old files.</p>
<p class="see"><a href="/power-bi-migration">See Power BI migration</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><LineIcon name="decision" />
<h2>Acquisition Performance Visibility</h2>
<p>After a buy, the buyer and the company need one picture of performance. The work is a gap analysis and a roadmap through the first hundred days.</p>
<p class="see"><a href="/acquisition-performance-visibility">See acquisition performance visibility</a></p>
</article>
</div>
<h2 class="industry-head">By the team that owns the meeting</h2>
<div class="cards-2">
<article class="card"><h2>Power BI for manufacturing</h2>
<p>Shop-floor numbers and finance numbers are in one report, so the plant meeting and the finance meeting are looking at the same file.</p>
<p class="see"><a href="/power-bi-for-manufacturing">See Power BI for manufacturing</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><h2>Power BI for Finance</h2>
<p>The close, profit and loss, variance, and cash are on numbers a leader will sign.</p>
<p class="see"><a href="/power-bi-for-finance">See Power BI for finance</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><h2>Power BI for supply chain</h2>
<p>Inventory and on-time delivery are in the same report finance already uses.</p>
<p class="see"><a href="/power-bi-for-supply-chain">See Power BI for supply chain</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><h2>Power BI for Quality</h2>
<p>Scrap, yield, and customer returns are in the Monday pack, alongside the numbers finance already reviews.</p>
<p class="see"><a href="/power-bi-for-quality">See Power BI for quality</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><h2>Power BI for HR</h2>
<p>Headcount, labor, and people costs tie back to profit and loss.</p>
<p class="see"><a href="/power-bi-for-hr">See Power BI for HR</a></p>
</article>
<article class="card"><h2>Power BI for Sales</h2>
<p>Pipeline and bookings that finance will accept are on the same definitions as the books.</p>
<p class="see"><a href="/power-bi-for-sales">See Power BI for sales</a></p>
</article>
</div>
</div></section>
<section class="band band-cta" aria-labelledby="cta-heading">
  <div class="wrap">
    <p class="kicker">Next step</p>
    <h2 id="cta-heading">Book a Session</h2>
    <p class="lede">Tell us which report or meeting is stuck. We will name a practical next step.</p>
    <p class="hero-actions"><a class="btn" href="/contact">Book a Session</a></p>
  </div>
</section>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
